course: dictionary
lesson: 3848
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word foul can describe a smell, the weather, or an action that breaks the rules in a game. Context tells you which meaning is right, so look at the words around it first.
explain: «The bin gave off a foul smell.» The word smell is the clue, so foul means very dirty or unpleasant. Check it by swapping in «a dirty smell»: it still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: «The referee blew the whistle for a foul.» The game and the whistle are the clues. In sport, a foul is an action that breaks the rules, like tripping another player. The meaning is different here, so always check the context again.
fact: Foul can be an adjective, a noun or a verb.
fact: «Foul» means very dirty, smelly or unpleasant, as in «a foul smell».
fact: In sport, a foul is an action that breaks the rules, like tripping or pushing another player.
fact: «Foul weather» means very bad weather, and «foul language» means rude words.
fact: «Fall foul of» means get into trouble with someone.
exercise: «The bin gave off a foul smell.» What does foul mean here? | *Very dirty or unpleasant | Cold and wet | Brand new and shiny | Loud and noisy
exercise: «The referee blew the whistle for a foul.» In sport, what is a foul? | A goal scored from far away | A short rest in the game | *An action that breaks the rules | A cheer from the crowd
exercise: «The sailors waited for the foul weather to pass.» What does foul weather mean? | *Very bad weather | Snow that is soft and fresh | Clear and calm skies | Gentle breeze and warm sun
test: «She used foul language, so her teacher was not pleased.» What does foul language mean? | Sweet sounds | *Rude words | Quiet singing | Lovely poems
test: «Dogs must not foul the park.» In this sentence, foul means | To win a prize | *To make something dirty | To sing loudly | To tidy up
exam: Jayden meets the word foul in a sentence about a football match and is not sure what it means. What helps him most? | *Reading the words around it, like the game and the rules | Guessing without reading the sentence | Skipping the sentence and never coming back to it | Looking only at the page number
